# interplay_memlive_held_discard_retarget: An exec that reads the four kinds of object (a shared and a private buffer, a private heap's buffer, a texture), all made and read before, waits on the gate while the worker FIFO (child 2) discards them (63) and the guest points their leaves at other pages. Released with flags 0 and then again with invalidateHost, it shows what each setup makes again over the new pages: a discard defers the rebinding to the next exec that pages the object, and what pages it is the setup's (the retarget_discard scenario's table, here decided at release time).
